{"question_id": "afdc33df", "type": "single-session-preference", "label": false, "judge": "No.", "question": "My kitchen's becoming a bit of a mess again. Any tips for keeping it clean?", "gold": "The user would prefer responses that acknowledge and build upon their existing efforts to organize their kitchen, such as utilizing their new utensil holder to keep countertops clutter-free. They would also appreciate tips that address their concern for maintaining their granite surface, particularly around the sink area. Preferred responses would provide practical and actionable steps to maintain cleanliness, leveraging the user's current tools and setup. They might not prefer generic or vague ", "hypothesis": "To keep your kitchen clean and organized, especially since you've been using it for various dishes like Japchae, here are some tailored tips for you:\n\n1. **Clean as You Go**: While cooking, try to clean up any spills or messes immediately. This will prevent them from piling up and becoming overwhelming later.\n\n2. **Daily Quick Clean**: Set aside 10-15 minutes each day to tidy up your kitchen. Wipe down counters, put away any items left out, and do a quick sweep of the floor.\n\n3. **Organize Utensils and Tools**: Since you have a new utensil holder, make sure to keep it organized by grouping similar items together. This will make it easier to find what you need and keep the countertops clutter-free.\n\n4. **Use Storage Solutions**: Utilize bins or baskets for storing items like spices, oils, or cooking tools. Label them for easy access and to maintain organization.\n\n5. **Plan Your Meals**: Since you're using Plan to Eat, plan your meals for the week. This will help you minimize food waste ", "judge_model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "provider": "OpenAI"}
