{"question_id": "505af2f5", "type": "single-session-preference", "label": true, "judge": "Yes.", "question": "I was thinking of trying a new coffee creamer recipe. Any recommendations?", "gold": "The user would prefer responses that suggest variations on their existing almond milk, vanilla extract, and honey creamer recipe or new ideas that align with their goals of reducing sugar intake and saving money. They might not prefer responses that recommend commercial creamer products or recipes that are high in sugar or expensive.", "hypothesis": "Since you've been making your own flavored creamer with almond milk, vanilla extract, and honey, here\u2019s a new recipe idea that builds on that while keeping it healthy:\n\n**Cinnamon Almond Milk Creamer**\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- 1 cup unsweetened almond milk (or your preferred milk)\n- 1-2 tablespoons maple syrup or a low-calorie sweetener like stevia (adjust to taste)\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n- 1 teaspoon ground cinnamon\n- A pinch of salt\n\n**Instructions:**\n1. In a small saucepan, combine the almond milk, maple syrup (or sweetener), vanilla extract, ground cinnamon, and salt.\n2. Heat the mixture over medium heat until warm, but do not boil.\n3. Stir well to combine all the ingredients.\n4. Remove from heat and let it cool slightly.\n5. Pour the creamer into a clean glass jar or container and store it in the refrigerator for up to a week.\n\n**Tips:**\n- You can also experiment by adding other spices like nutmeg or cardamom for a different flavor profile.\n- If you want a creamier texture, consid", "judge_model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "provider": "OpenAI"}
